  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and preferring the lottery with higher variance. However, the individual did not mention variance, risk spread, or dispersion of outcomes. Instead, they focused on the probability of winning (i.e., the chance of receiving a non-zero payoff), which is a different criterion. The individual preferred Lottery B due to its higher probability of winning (90% vs. 45%), which is contrary to the variance-based reason (which would favor Lottery A). The information considered by the individual (probability of winning) does not align with the variance calculation, and the justification (higher chance of winning) contradicts the rule of the decision reason (preferring higher variance). Therefore, the individual did not use the variance-based reason to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
